On Saturday night, September 25, 1993, Greg Naber passed away at his
home in Renton, Washington as a result of a heart attack.  Greg was 38
years old.

Over the years, Greg impressed me with his willingness to help others. 
While my association with him mainly centered around computer-related
activities, I had opportunities to see his kindness in other areas.
He was a dear friend.

Greg was the driving force behind getting the GIF files of missing kids
distributed between the Fidonet network and the Internet ftp sites, as
well as helping gate the Usenet newsgroup alt.missing-kids in and out
of Fidonet's MISSING-KIDS echo.

Locally, Greg's expertise and willingness to help others set up and
distribute the Linux operating system and the Waffle bbs package helped
bring new areas of communications to many.

Greg Naber has helped me in various ways since halcyon's inception.  He
recently took over operation of our Network Operations Center, and his
desire to learn and his experience will be deeply missed.

Funeral arrangements are pending at Edline-Yawn Funeral Home, in Kent,
WA, (206) 852-1707.  A date and time for services will be announced
tomorrow.  Flowers, cards, and memorials may be sent to the funeral
home at 424 W. Meeker St., Kent, WA 98042.
