        address set by a compile time or LILO command line option)
        any port mapped (all 8 ports) NCR5380 board (This "should"
	work with many of the cheap NCR5380 boards out there, anything
	not mapping all eight ports at contiguous addresses (ie, the
	PAS-16) won't work.

2. The low level code can automatically perform a REQUEST SENSE
        command for commands that terminate with a CHECK CONDITION
        status.  This is necessary to insure that another command
        to the same target/LUN is not executed (clearing the 
        contingent alligence condition) before the REQUEST SENSE.

3.  The code to autodetect the IRQ line has been moved to the generic
        driver from the Trantor wrapper.

4.  Preliminary support for linked commands is there (pending upper 
	level code)

