CircleMUD is a multi-user game server designed to allow players from around
the globe to connect to the server and interact with each other in an
environment modelled after a Dungeons & Dragons type world.

CircleMUD is Linux-compatible, hence the posting to this newsgroup.  Linux
compatibility is activated by making a simple change to the Makefile.

CircleMUD 2.11 is now available for anonymous ftp at its official site --
ftp.cs.jhu.edu:pub/CircleMUD.  It should also be availabe at tsx-11.mit.edu
in the next week to ten days.

Most changes in 2.11 from 2.10 are bug fixes.  There is very little code
which is completely new, but all bugs reported with 2.10 have been fixed.
The big ones are:

   -- SET FILE bug
   -- SIGBUS/unaligned data errors under SunOS and other OS's
   -- Move limit modifier bug
   -- wrist-wearing bug
   -- Compilation problems with utility.c under some operating systems

The only notable change is that the hit_limit, move_limit, and mana_limit
functions have been removed (for many reasons).  From the players' point of
view, this means that a character no longer gains movement points with age.
Hit, move, and mana gain speeds are still a function of age, however.

Please, keep those bug reports coming -- I don't actually run a copy of
CircleMUD personally, so I depend on your bug reports to iron out the
last few bugs which always seem to be there.

Jeremy

